  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "heading_gap",
      "source": "SCUT commands.py:577–604; saved rough_dash env.yaml:1749–1769",
      "actual": "Heading target uniform [-pi,pi], Bernoulli rel_heading_envs .5, stiffness5, yaw clip ±2pi. Source uses actual robot.data.heading_w. Only normal non-special heading IDs are processed; standing velocity zeroing is last. v24 currently maps neither heading target nor heading closed loop.",
      "decision": "Fits native35D/6action as command-generation state only: actor sees resolved yaw speed, never absolute world heading. It still needs separately saved target/mask and per-resample RNG/reset ownership for production; pure resolver is not runtime integration."
    },
    {
      "id": "wrap_boundary",
      "source": "inspected native utils/math.py:100–122",
      "actual": "wrap=(angle+pi)%(2pi), then where(wrap==0 and angle>0, pi, wrap-pi); +pi→+pi, -pi→-pi. Original source delegates to its IsaacLab math_utils; this audit binds the inspected local dependency, not an unproven historical IsaacLab version."
    },
    {
      "id": "special_assignment",
      "source": "commands.py:275–285,344–394,419–450,493–552",
      "actual": "Enabled from iteration0 until infinity. At resample, standing draw first; only remaining IDs with elapsed episode≥5s are special candidates. One uniform variate assigns at most one disjoint cumulative bucket after random mode order. Segments are weighted by interval length. Saved require_stable=false; no extra stable gate is appropriate. Delayed and leftover normal IDs delegate to base sampler."
    },
    {
      "id": "source_rates_and_double_standing",
      "source": "saved profiles + commands.py:497–552 + inspected native velocity_command.py:159–174",
      "actual": "rough_dash conditional ready/non-terrain rates: rotate .9*(.15+.15)=.27, high translation .9*.2=.18, special all-zero .9*.1=.09, ordinary leftover .36. Current inspected base resamples standing on leftover, adding .036: total zero .226. Before special-ready, .1+.9*.1=.19. rough_rotation_stair high translation .27, rotation .27, zero .136. These describe source subclass plus inspected base at resample; upstream historical base version is not independently pinned.",
      "limits": "Not global lane occupancy, not elapsed-time probability, not measured actual-v24 command histogram. Current native ordinary sampler has one .1 standing draw."
    },
    {
      "id": "terrain_priority",
      "source": "SCUT V13 env.py:347–374",
      "actual": "Caller disables source special modes before and after state-machine command update, applies terrain overrides and restores heading closed-loop yaw. Per-step disable and source heading/nonheading terrain logic cannot be copied as one-time flags. Native explicit eight small-stair rows preserve5–40mm geometry; heading prototype excludes those eight rows until their reset/heading-specific override semantics are designed."
    },
    {
      "id": "native_overlay",
      "source": "runtime recipe domains.<domain>.patch scene_groups and scut_reuse_candidate.mapped_groups",
      "actual": "All four use rough_dash. Overlay of ready SCUT selector onto24 ordinary groups adds conditional high-special .45*S while native dedicated high families remain. It duplicates high-motion training emphasis. Existing ordinary normal mixture already spans vx±2.7/yaw±2pi, so high-family labels plus selector fractions are not an exact physical speed histogram.",
      "standing_stop_implication": "If only changing selection within24 ordinary groups, explicit standing/release-stop fractions remain exact; do not claim they are diluted. Source extra zero mode actually increases ordinary exact-zero probability under this base. Renormalizing all rows or adding another pool can dilute anchors and must be avoided."
    },
    {
      "id": "minimal_heading_route",
      "source": "native skill_commands.py + env command projection",
      "decision": "Independent opt-in ordinary-only heading resolver is feasible without special selector or quota changes. Preserve fixed stand, start-stop/release-stop/spin-translate/recovery/requested-jump/nativehigh and explicit terrain sequences. Preserve native [vx,yaw,height] ABI; standing zeroes velocities, never height. Keep native slew/feasibility and difficulty clamps. Equation agreement is before these transforms, not bit-identical final-command distribution."
    },
    {
      "id": "minimal_special_route",
      "decision": "For true SCUT special proportions, replace the ordinary+nativehigh locomotion sampling population as a single explicitly budgeted manager/pool; do not stack a second selector. Keep stand/release-stop/recovery/jump protection and native challenge quota deliberate. Source maxvx3/maxyaw14.137 does not cover current native challenges vx5/yaw18.85. There is no authorization or evidence here to change frozen recipes or queue."
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanical_exclusions",
      "source": "saved rough_dash env.yaml:815–820,2389,2427,2527–2528; source observation concatenation3198–3213",
      "actual": "Source also declares35actor/6action but controls a distinct gimbal and has different leg geometry, state78, mode-context semantics; current native critic/interface differ. No heading_target/world-heading actor field. Saved special jump_takeoff_enabled=false in every mode; retain that disability for source-special transplant, do not infer native active-jump disable. Do not copy source gimbal torque/PID, raycast, geometry, privileged state or exported weights mechanically."
    }
  ],
